Subject: [PATCH] Model StickS3 M5PM1 I2C IAP and BOOT_OUT sampling

The M5PM1 normal I2C slave switches to its IAP bootloader address after
the updater's entry transaction. Model write-enable, contiguous app
pages, CRC verification and return to normal addressing. Keep the
PM1 image separate from ESP32 Flash and from the live PM1 register model.

The StickS3 also wires the PM1 BOOT_OUT to ESP32-S3 GPIO0. The PM1
pulses it across a cold reset, where the SoC latches the ROM strap.
Other PM1 boards retain their existing lifecycle.

Source: M5PM1 Datasheet rev 1.8 (Download Flowchart), K150 StickS3
schematic rev 0.6, and the official M5PM1-O updater I2C data path.
Native-only layer, apply after 0170.

